    "3.9": {
      "file": "content/circ/ch03-b.js",
      "hash": "038a8547fc6c591f0ab5fe8277a083d45ea78f079ec4fe0607515644c8b1f56a",
      "fields": {
        "statement": {
          "before": "A two-port is a linear network accessed through two pairs of terminals (ports), each carrying equal and opposite currents ($I_1$, $I_2$ into the ports, $V_1$, $V_2$ the port voltages). Because the network is linear, any two of the four quantities determine the other two, and the relation is a $2\\times2$ matrix: the impedance matrix $\\mathbf z$ ($\\mathbf V = \\mathbf z\\mathbf I$), the admittance matrix $\\mathbf y$ ($\\mathbf I = \\mathbf y\\mathbf V$), the hybrid matrix $\\mathbf h$, and the transmission (ABCD) matrix, $\\begin{pmatrix} V_1\\\\ I_1\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} A&B\\\\ C&D\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix} V_2\\\\ -I_2\\end{pmatrix}$. Each entry is measured with the other port short- or open-circuited. If two two-ports are cascaded (port 2 of the first = port 1 of the second), their ABCD matrices multiply. The two-port is reciprocal when $z_{12} = z_{21}$, equivalently $AD - BC = 1$.",
          "after": "A two-port is a linear network accessed through two pairs of terminals (ports), each carrying equal and opposite currents ($I_1$, $I_2$ into the ports, $V_1$, $V_2$ the port voltages). The port variables obey linear constraints. A chosen pair determines the other pair only when the corresponding elimination is nonsingular; the resulting relation is a $2\\times2$ matrix: the impedance matrix $\\mathbf z$ ($\\mathbf V = \\mathbf z\\mathbf I$), the admittance matrix $\\mathbf y$ ($\\mathbf I = \\mathbf y\\mathbf V$), the hybrid matrix $\\mathbf h$, and the transmission (ABCD) matrix, $\\begin{pmatrix} V_1\\\\ I_1\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} A&B\\\\ C&D\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix} V_2\\\\ -I_2\\end{pmatrix}$. Each entry is measured with the other port short- or open-circuited. If two two-ports are cascaded (port 2 of the first = port 1 of the second), their ABCD matrices multiply. Where the respective parameter descriptions exist, reciprocity is tested by $z_{12}=z_{21}$ in the impedance form or $AD-BC=1$ in the transmission form, with the stated current convention.",
          "expectedHash": "d52a29e0b06f67263c064b983bfebb7e39a86fbb59b48a5bbcce8dac3be5fb3a"
        }
      }
    },
